# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Cloudflare evaluates _redirects BEFORE serving static assets (unlike Netlify),
# so a naked `/* / 302` rule would catch even `/` and loop on itself.
# Pin every known path with a 200 rewrite first so the catch-all only sees
# unknown paths. First match wins.
#
# When adding a new page (e.g. /docs), add a matching rewrite line BEFORE the
# catch-all and rerun seo-consistency-check.

/             /index.html          200
/about        /about/index.html    200
/about/       /about/index.html    200
/privacy      /privacy/index.html  200
/privacy/     /privacy/index.html  200
/terms        /terms/index.html    200
/terms/       /terms/index.html    200
/favicon.svg  /favicon.svg         200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml         200
/robots.txt   /robots.txt          200

# Unknown paths (/ko, /blog/foo, etc) → home, 302 temporary.
/*            /                    302
